    "result_text": "All tests pass (the suite consists of `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are helpers). `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` following the codebase's established owner-policy pattern, keeping structural impact low by putting the new behavior in its own small, cohesive unit rather than growing an existing method or class.\n\n**New isolated unit** \u2014 `service/OwnerNamesakePolicy.java`: a self-contained static helper (WMC_other = 0) mirroring `OwnerCustomerCodePolicy`/`OwnerTelephonePolicy`. It counts existing owners sharing the same `firstName` + `lastName` case-insensitively (via `equalsIgnoreCase`) before the create and sets it on the owner.\n\n**Minimal edits to existing code:**\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 one import + one line in `addOwner`, called before `saveOwner` so the count reflects state *before* this create.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `namesakeCount` field with a getter/setter, placed beside the sibling `customerCode`/`householdId` accessors. MapStruct maps it to/from the DTO automatically by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, minimum 0) to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto`.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `namesake_count INTEGER` column so the value persists and is visible on the subsequent `GET`.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 added the trailing seed value to the 10 positional owner inserts (required by the new column).\n\nThe test creates two owners sharing `firstName`+`lastName` (distinct addresses avoid the household 409), then `GET`s the second and asserts `namesakeCount == 1` \u2014 green.",
